ie n Clark acting returning officer for  the Somerton and Froome constituency  declare that the total number of votes  cast across the Somerton and Froome  constituency at the UK parliamentary  election on the 8th of June 2017 was  sixty three thousand nine hundred ninety  six the total number of ballot papers  rejected was 104 the total number of  votes given to each candidate was as  follows Mark David Harry Blackburn  Liberal Democrats 13,000 325 Shaun Adam  Dromgoole Labour Party 10,000 998  Richard Thomas hadwin independent 991  Theo Simon Green Party 2347 David John  Warburton the Conservative Party  candidate 36,000 231 therefore I gave  public notice that David John more  burden is duly elected as the Member of  Parliament for the Somerton and Froome  constituency  thank you very much can I first thank  all the officials and all the people  who've worked so hard throughout the  night and the police for keeping us safe  and for facilitating the democratic  process it looks like a rather  extraordinary in perhaps a bit  interesting nights is unfold it  unfolding across the country but once  again I'm deeply honored to be able to  play my part and go to Westminster to  take up a position on the back bench to  fight for our parts of Somerset but I'm  only here because of the efforts of  others and I must thank David Norris my  chairman my agent who's done a great job  and my tremendous association the  legions of volunteers many which are are  here and have been working here tonight  and I must particularly thank David and  Russell who have made the past few weeks  as near to a delight as it's possible  with an election campaign but most of  all I must thank my wife Harriet's who's  coped with all the slings and arrows of  the last few weeks and thank you also to  the other candidates it's again been a  pleasure to work alongside and to get to  know them in what sometimes has been a  rather unpleasant campaign I have to say  unlike the last election the campaign  locally although mostly friendly and  positive has also had an underlying  sense of sneering sort of anger so that  some points of view have been stamped on  and closed down in the name of some kind  of confetti moral outrage only one view  is allowed a different perspective is  morally wrong and so abuse vandalism and  hatred is fully justified and this  sickness leads to a bad place and it  should have no place in today's world I  hope it now dies the death that it  deserves  the last few years I think have seen  enough political division remain errs  and levers labour and conservative now  is becoming very two-party about even  young and old so we must build bridges  and cooperate democratically so we  achieved the best for the future for all  of us I think it's perhaps the greatest  privilege that can be lent to a person  to be asked by local people to represent  them in the House of Commons I will try  to justify that trust thank you
 

